1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,440
Many years ago, mankind faced a divine fury.

2
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,840
In an event known as the Day of the Cataclysm,

3
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,040
our entire world was burned.

4
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:20,880
The fire raged with an intensity

5
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:23,120
that threatened to reduce mankind to ash.

6
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,500
The places they lived, the languages they spoke,

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,240
the culture they had built,

8
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:30,480
none could escape its wrath.

9
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:52,440
Haran has returned to the flame.

10
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,700
He died a martyr.

11
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:00,880
It was a small price to pay for the birth of a new demon.

12
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:02,560
No regrets.

13
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,860
Also, the boy from Company 8 with an Edole burst

14
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,760
experienced an Edole link with the demon.

15
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,760
Then that settles it.

16
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:17,080
Yes, we must acquire him.

17
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:19,080
For the evangelist wills it.

18
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:22,140
It's a waste for the Fire Force to have an asset like that.

19
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:25,500
There may be more to this than it seems.

20
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,480
I'll go along next time.

21
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:35,220
A new team member coming out of nowhere?

22
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,440
It seems kind of sudden, don't you think?

23
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:40,320
Hajima a strong-armed one of their people through

24
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,600
since the 8th doesn't have its own science team.

25
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,020
They're plotting something.

26
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:46,840
That's a little harsh.

27
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,700
After the whole evangelist incident,

28
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,760
every company is under Imperial order

29
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,300
to step up their scientific investigations, right?

30
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,860
I know we've been lagging a bit in that area,

31
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,540
but we were searching out new members.

32
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:01,760
In the meantime, Captain Hibana has been providing us

33
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,140
with all the support we need.

34
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,960
Yeah, but that's a bit of a bad habit to get into,

35
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,360
and I'm sure a captain like her

36
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:08,780
has plenty on her plate already.

37
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,960
Hajima saw a problem and offered me as a solution.

38
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:16,100
Therefore, I will now be serving

39
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,900
as Special Fire Force Company 8's head scientist.

40
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,100
The name's Victor Leaked.

41
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:52,840
Take what you got and leave now.

42
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,540
You're wearing out, you're welcome.

43
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,440
No one here wants to see you, hear you.

44
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:00,860
Think that you won from day one,

45
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:02,800
but then the devil will come.

46
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,480
You know just why he wants you, don't you?

47
00:03:06,700 --> 00:03:10,280
You're crooked, desire, left us in history.

48
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:14,300
Misguided, defighted, in the part of the reason.

49
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:18,740
You started a fighter, you're gonna watch it burn.

50
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:21,640
Try to save yourself like you always do.

51
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:27,520
Every bridge we bow, you think it's just a burn it down.

52
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:32,500
Just burn it down, when everything is gone.

53
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:37,240
You wish you only hurt us out, hurt us out.

54
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,120
Screaming, METE!

55
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,000
METE!

56
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,220
METE!

57
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,140
METE!

58
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,060
METE!

59
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,940
METE!

60
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,040
METE!

61
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,040
METE!

62
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:59,340
It smells like a rat if you ask me.

63
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:04,220
A proper Fire Force salute should be performed with the right hand, not the left one.

64
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,440
Oh, uh, not really my thing?

65
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,300
I'm sorry.

66
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,100
Oh, scientists, right?

67
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,500
Head in the clouds.

68
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,000
Oh.

69
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,080
I don't, my curiosity!

70
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:16,940
I don't have to see you.

71
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,160
What are you doing?

72
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,000
Show me.

73
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:19,940
Show me.

74
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:23,700
Don't get touchy-feely with him.

75
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,080
Yes, ma'am.

76
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,460
My boy!

77
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:31,500
Victor leaked.

78
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:32,940
Let's see.

79
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:36,220
Advanced placement into Tokyo Imperial University.

80
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:38,420
Graduated at the top of your class.

81
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:42,120
Headed the applied pyrokinesiology lab at Hyjima Heavy Industries.

82
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,140
I must admit, it's quite the resume.

83
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:45,720
Hmm.

84
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,040
What can I say?

85
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,280
I'm brilliant.

86
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,560
More like suspiciously brilliant.

87
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,920
This place is a dump.

88
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:54,600
Why would you want to work here?

89
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:58,560
Hyjima kept me cooped up in my lab all the time, and it was starting to get stale.

90
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:02,060
I thought if I joined an outfit closer to the action, I might be able to get some intriguing

91
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,040
new data out of the front lines, so to speak.

92
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,560
If I cause any trouble, you can kick me out.

93
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,560
But at least let me join for now.

94
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,500
Looking at your staff list, I'm a little worried.

95
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,640
You guys don't have an engineer yet, do you?

96
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:20,360
It's nice that you have a researcher now, but are any of you qualified to service your vehicle?

97
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,700
You gotta take care of that stuff.

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,480
Yeah, that's on the agenda.

99
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,320
We have someone in mind already.

100
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,240
Lieutenant, have you been able to reach him?

101
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,060
Vulcan?

102
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,300
He hasn't replied.

103
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,500
You're trying to recruit Vulcan?

104
00:05:32,620 --> 00:05:34,260
Are you taking this seriously at all?

105
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,560
Should I know him?

106
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:38,760
The point is that nobody can recruit him.

107
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:43,040
Hyjima, the special fire force, he turns them all away in an instant.

108
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:47,140
But I'll tell you, Vulcan's the real deal.

109
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,680
He's a true god of the forge, just like his namesake.

110
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:58,280
We may have to make a personal trip to his workshop if we want to get through to him.

111
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:00,900
I don't think that's gonna work out for you.

112
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:05,960
He hates Hyjima with a passion, and he hates the fire force as much for working with him.

113
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:07,880
He'll send you packing like everyone else.

114
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,220
Okay, then.

115
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:14,020
Shinra, I want you to head to Vulcan's workshop, take Iris and Arthur with you.

116
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:18,820
Before we move forward with anything, I need to know if this guy's company ate material.

117
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,000
You think we're good to make that call?

118
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,760
Why do you want to send us three?

119
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,660
Vulcan is about your age, so you might get along.

120
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:29,420
Keep it casual, keep it honest, and don't let him think you're trying too hard.

121
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:30,620
Yes, sir!

122
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:37,260
I don't want this to be too formal, so it's better if you go in your civvies.

123
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:40,380
That doesn't mean you need to be cagey about who you are, though.

124
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:43,020
If we come across as deceptive, he won't trust us.

125
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,460
Just try to say hello.

126
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,540
If all the stories are true, that may be hard enough.

127
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,340
We'll show him some guts!

128
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:54,020
The other company's tried to tempt Vulcan with promises of money.

129
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,160
Or status.

130
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,120
The Eighth is just sending kids.

131
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,840
I told you, Vulcan loathes the Fire Force.

132
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:03,020
This is a total waste of your time.

133
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:05,080
We're trying to change the world here.

134
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,340
We gotta do the impossible.

135
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,600
Let's try and see what happens.

136
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:13,060
I just got here and things are getting interesting already.

137
00:07:15,140 --> 00:07:17,100
Well, this should be as good a test as any.

138
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:19,900
Let's see if you can help us reach our goals or not.

139
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,060
Company Eight.

140
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,520
I've seen that animal in a picture book.

141
00:07:29,700 --> 00:07:31,380
The big one with the long snout.

142
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,980
Yeah, it's called an elephant, right?

143
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,140
That's it.

144
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,200
I think.

145
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,960
This place is really something.

146
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:40,860
Excuse me!

147
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:45,940
Maybe he's not at home.

148
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,980
Or he's just ignoring us.

149
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:49,700
I am the Night King!

150
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,140
Arthur Boyle!

151
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:52,420
Fire Soldier!

152
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,680
How audacious of you to disrespect the Night King!

153
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,940
It's the Fire Soldier part he didn't like!

154
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:00,900
Get lost!

155
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:04,580
Ow-hey!

156
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,320
Slow-witted dolt.

157
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,040
Ow!

158
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:16,360
Stop screwing with us and come out!

159
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,940
You think your feeble projectiles intimidate me?

160
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:20,860
Um, hello.

161
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,020
Can I help you?

162
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,700
Ah, Atom.

163
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:32,080
I'm sorry for being so rude.

164
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:34,460
We're here from Special Fire Force Company Eight.

165
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:35,980
I'm Shinra Kusakabe.

166
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,540
First Class Fire Soldier.

167
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:40,340
And I'm a hero, too.

168
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,720
Another visit from another Fire Force Company, huh?

169
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:46,840
You're here to recruit the Master, but he won't let you in, I assume.

170
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,680
Hello? Master?

171
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,020
I've returned with the parts you asked for.

172
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:58,540
Yeah, I told you not to call me Master, remember?

173
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:00,900
It's either Vulcan or Dirtbag.

174
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:01,960
Take your pick.

175
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:03,480
Vulcan, then.

176
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:07,040
But anyway, um, the parts that you needed are in that bag.

177
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,340
Hold on, Dirtbag!

178
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:10,820
Ah!

179
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,040
Aw.

180
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,200
Enough like the can't-

181
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:14,460
Huh?

182
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,160
What?

183
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:17,180
There's a second can of salient?

184
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:21,280
I have nothing to say to you Fire Soldiers.

185
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,120
Buzz off!

186
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,960
He really doesn't like us, huh?

187
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:28,180
Although I guess we were warned.

188
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:33,880
We didn't even say anything, and he's already picking a fight.

189
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:34,980
Let's go.

190
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:36,460
This isn't gonna work.

191
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,060
Hold on a sec.

192
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:43,320
I'll hear you out, if you guys will talk to me.

193
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:52,160
It almost sounds like he's playing drums in there.

194
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:55,980
Did Vulcan make all this crazy stuff lying around?

195
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,560
Yeah, pretty much.

196
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:00,800
There's projects from his father and grandfather, too.

197
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,560
Wait, and you bring him parts?

198
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,460
Is he forcing you to do all his busy work?

199
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:07,260
He doesn't have to force me.

200
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,040
I want to.

201
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:11,940
It's not like official, but, uh, I'm sort of Vulcan's apprentice.

202
00:10:13,020 --> 00:10:16,480
I've always liked tinkering with machines, and I admire Vulcan's work.

203
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:19,100
So I asked him if I could lend a hand around the workshop.

204
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:23,540
That was the plan, but I'm mostly running errands now.

205
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,820
So did something happen to change things?

206
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,320
Vulcan's talent is the real deal.

207
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:35,860
His work shows precision, speed, and above all else, creativity.

208
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:39,580
He's the ultimate technician, with no weak points.

209
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:43,060
I'm not really into the whole skull thing, but whatever.

210
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:50,800
Anyway, as you can imagine, he's in high demand, from Heijima and you guys.

211
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,400
But Vulcan turns everyone away on the spot.

212
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:59,560
Heijima wasn't too happy about this, of course, so they pulled some strings.

213
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:03,080
And now, no more merchants will work with him.

214
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:05,240
He can't get materials anywhere.

215
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:13,100
But I've been able to get him most of the parts he needs by running around to different junk shops.

216
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,140
I guess I'd hate Heijima, too, if I were him.

217
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:17,720
I don't know.

218
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:20,840
He hates Heijima and the Fire Force a lot.

219
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,720
I haven't heard the details, but it's quite the grudge.

220
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:26,620
Trust me, we aren't like the other companies.

221
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,520
You have my word on that.

222
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:33,220
Please, can you at least ask Vulcan to hear us out?

223
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:34,540
Just this once.

224
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:37,560
Maybe you're right.

225
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,760
I have to admit, you're nothing like the others who came to recruit him.

226
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,680
I'll take you in.

227
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,180
It's worth a shot.

228
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:57,800
Should we just barge in without asking?

229
00:11:58,340 --> 00:12:01,160
Vulcan might yell at me about it, but it'll be fine.

230
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:06,660
Wait, it was a machine all along.

231
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:08,760
Owie!

232
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:10,260
Another one?

233
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,020
How many?

234
00:12:12,260 --> 00:12:14,480
Actually, that one was thrown by Lisa.

235
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,780
She lives here with Vulcan.

236
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,500
Yeah, come on!

237
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:21,280
You know better than to let the Fire Force in here!

238
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:23,640
My arm, you're breaking it!

239
00:12:29,780 --> 00:12:32,520
I don't know about all the banging, but he's fast.

240
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,680
I've never seen that technique before.

241
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:45,040
All right, it's done!

242
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:48,100
Why would you kick something you just made across the floor?

243
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,100
What if it breaks?

244
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:52,840
A machine that breaks from one kick is defective, far as I'm concerned.

245
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,320
Hey, you little rats!

246
00:12:54,460 --> 00:12:55,760
Who invited you in here?

247
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,360
We want to talk, that's all.

248
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:58,700
Hey, yeah!

249
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,740
What are you doing?

250
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,300
Bring some drinks already!

251
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:05,260
Oh, thank you.

252
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:06,600
Yeah, right!

253
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:09,600
Just five minutes, okay?

254
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,860
I heard enough from the Fire Force to last a lifetime.

255
00:13:13,180 --> 00:13:15,060
So get your ass out of my shop!

256
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:17,180
Moron.

257
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:22,440
Vul, looks like he's back.

258
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:27,800
I'll handle it.

259
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,220
Are you okay alone?

260
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:33,800
It'll be fine.

261
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:47,420
That's the Captain of the Third.

262
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,780
Their company is in tight with Heijima.

263
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,640
Does that mean they're gonna nab Vulcan before us?

264
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,320
No way.

265
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:55,840
If Vulcan goes with them,

266
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:58,060
there's no way his dream will ever come true.

267
00:13:58,060 --> 00:14:11,620
How has business been these days?

268
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:14,100
Slow, it seems.

269
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,220
You still have a fondness for animals,

270
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,760
like when you were a child.

271
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:22,160
That was a dirty trick you pulled!

272
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,980
I know you're the one who cut me off from my suppliers!

273
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:26,340
You think that's gonna work?

274
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:30,300
I needed to teach you it takes more than blueprints to build something.

275
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,820
Stop being stubborn and join us.

276
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:37,080
I assure you, you'll have all the materials you could ever dream of.

277
00:14:37,560 --> 00:14:40,480
I wouldn't even change a light bulb for your filthy company!

278
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,700
This is your final warning, Vulcan.

279
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:47,820
If you fail to heed it, you can only blame yourself.

280
00:14:48,560 --> 00:14:49,840
What, you gonna kill me?

281
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:52,240
Like you did with my dad and my granddad?

282
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:56,960
What are you talking about?

283
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,660
Piss off, you backstabber!

284
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:01,260
Such a pity.

285
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:06,960
All your talent wasting away in this scrapyard when you could accomplish so much more.

286
00:15:08,220 --> 00:15:11,720
Speaking of wasteful, your plan with the animals will never work.

287
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,260
Shut up!

288
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,860
A child's dream.

289
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:19,220
You sold off all your dreams for money and power!

290
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,740
What the hell do you know?!

291
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:23,620
You're not being bold, you're being selfish.

292
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:28,700
If you offered your talents to the Empire, imagine how many lives could be saved.

293
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:31,060
Your dream is worthless.

294
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:33,700
It's too pathetic to even laugh at.

295
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,380
What's your problem?

296
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,960
I thought I told you to get out of here.

297
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,780
Sure it was smart to piss off Heijima like that?

298
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:46,040
It's not your problem either way.

299
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,600
Actually, it is.

300
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:51,660
The Eighth was formed to investigate the Fire Force from the inside.

301
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:55,800
We're not like the other companies who were tied down by big organizations.

302
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:58,620
The only thing we care about is helping people.

303
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:00,040
So talk to us.

304
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,360
Maybe we can help you too.

305
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:08,040
Who turned that thing on?

306
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:10,640
Oops.

307
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:12,920
Guess I must have touched it someplace weird.

308
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,080
We're having a serious conversation here.

309
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,940
Stop touching things in weird places.

310
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,280
What does this button do?

311
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:20,280
Nothing good.

312
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,080
Don't press it.

313
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:22,660
What's your deal?

314
00:16:25,780 --> 00:16:28,220
Hey, how do you get this thing to stop?

315
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:29,060
Don't ask me.

316
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:32,180
What's this one do?

317
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,900
Get away from there!

318
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:34,520
Boom.

319
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,840
The Allopants!

320
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,660
What does this little round guy do?

321
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,480
Don't you dare.

322
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,160
Oh, I'm sorry.

323
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:50,260
How do you guys even function?

324
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:51,340
You're totally nuts.

325
00:16:51,620 --> 00:16:53,680
And I'm supposed to believe you're fire soldiers?

326
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,400
All right, fine.

327
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:58,260
You're probably going to get in trouble if you go back empty-handed.

328
00:16:58,340 --> 00:16:58,760
Am I right?

329
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:03,920
I won't join your team, but I will show you something to make your trip worth it.

330
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,920
After that, you leave me alone.

331
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:07,740
I'm listening.

332
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:10,220
I haven't gotten to see this in a long time!

333
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:13,260
Hey, should I bring this with me or what?

334
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:14,520
Just put it down.

335
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:18,740
That's enough room.

336
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:20,460
So, what is it?

337
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:21,500
Some invention of yours?

338
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:25,980
When I was little, I made this with my dad and my granddad.

339
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:28,060
Now shut up and watch.

340
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:35,380
I want to make things people have never seen.

341
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:37,300
I won't settle for something ordinary.

342
00:17:50,620 --> 00:17:55,920
Not too bad, huh?

343
00:17:55,920 --> 00:18:00,680
Would you believe that there used to be over 1.7 million species of animals in the world?

344
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,920
This is unreal.

345
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:06,680
Those are elephants, aren't they?

346
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,400
What are those?

347
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:18,900
Migratory birds.

348
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:21,360
They used to fly from continent to continent.

349
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:25,480
But with the way things are now, there'd be nowhere left for them to go.

350
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:30,580
They don't understand this feeling.

351
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:35,580
But for some strange reason, I can't stop crying.

352
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:40,600
Amaterasu can only generate enough power for the Empire's people.

353
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:43,040
So I want to create a new energy source.

354
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:46,200
Something even stronger that can bring the whole world back.

355
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:50,720
And I'll bring all of the animals who went extinct back to life with it.

356
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:53,120
That's the dream I'm fighting for.

357
00:18:54,460 --> 00:18:57,780
This is someone who wants to use his power to save lives.

358
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,040
In a way no one else can.

359
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,760
Captain Obi, you had the right idea.

360
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:07,300
Vulcan is perfect for Company 8.

361
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:30,120
Every time I watch, it blows me away.

362
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,400
So, you guys, what did you think?

363
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,760
Honestly, it touched my heart.

364
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:35,980
So cool.

365
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:38,780
Listen, Vulcan.

366
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,700
I know you'd love it at Company 8.

367
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,200
Please stop by.

368
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,720
Just talk to our captain and you'll understand.

369
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:46,380
Sorry.

370
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:50,940
Nothing you say will ever convince me to side with anyone under Hajima's thumb.

371
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:54,280
I'll find my own way.

372
00:19:56,140 --> 00:19:57,620
Same thing every time.

373
00:19:58,020 --> 00:19:59,620
So, how did you meet Vulcan?

374
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,480
Both my parents died in a fire.

375
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,860
An infernal destroyed my life.

376
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:07,520
Later, my relatives died too.

377
00:20:08,060 --> 00:20:09,800
I was about to be put in a convent.

378
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:12,340
But the last thing I want to be is a nun.

379
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,720
Oh, I'm sorry.

380
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,660
You're not a nun, are you?

381
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:17,440
It's fine.

382
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:21,400
I ran away, straight off to nowhere.

383
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,660
I had nothing.

384
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:30,060
I wandered here to the scrapyard, looking for a place where I could stay out of the rain.

385
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,900
Then Vulcan found me and took me in.

386
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:38,340
He has a kind heart, huh?

387
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,300
Yeah, he does.

388
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:41,980
Too kind, maybe.

389
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:45,220
Vulcan will take in anyone who needs his help.

390
00:20:45,220 --> 00:20:46,960
And animals, too.

391
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,700
He will work hard to take care of all of them.

392
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:51,320
Whose grave is this?

393
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:53,180
Vulcan's father's.

394
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:54,840
And his grandfather's, too.

395
00:20:55,440 --> 00:20:57,580
Both of them went infernal at the same time.

396
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:00,140
That isn't something that happens often, right?

397
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:03,360
Vulcan thinks Giovanni had something to do with it.

398
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:07,220
And does he have a good reason to suspect him?

399
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:10,800
Vulcan's grandfather had taken on two apprentices.

400
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:15,420
One of them was Vulcan's father, and the other one was Giovanni.

401
00:21:16,360 --> 00:21:21,160
Right after his father and grandfather died in natural deaths, Giovanni went to work for

402
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:21,600
Heijima.

403
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,400
That's something that was forbidden by their master.

404
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,820
Oh, why was it forbidden?

405
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:28,580
Something with his family.

406
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:32,320
Apparently they have a bad history with Heijima going way back.

407
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:38,560
Nice chat, but I'd better get started on Vul's dinner.

408
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:42,180
I hate to say it, but you really should give up.

409
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,600
Sorry, I couldn't be more helpful.

410
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:45,800
Don't say that.

411
00:21:45,860 --> 00:21:46,320
We just need...

412
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:49,540
The time has come.

413
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:51,540
Vulcan must be killed.

414
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:58,000
It's that same feeling I had back in Asakusa.

415
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:02,620
That time, it was Lieutenant Conroe calling out for help.

416
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:06,620
This time, it's Dr. Giovanni out for blood.

417
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,820
Anyway, I think this is a bust.

418
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:11,680
Let's head back to the station and see what's next.

419
00:22:12,900 --> 00:22:15,280
We can't leave Vulcan on his own right now.

420
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:17,420
Call it my hero's intuition.

421
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,280
It's philosophy.

422
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:50,840
As you can follow atul.

423
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:53,260
We can't leave theQUE 학.

424
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:55,680
I don't know if you're under it.

425
00:22:55,680 --> 00:23:07,680
.

426
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,680
.

427
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:13,680
.

428
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:18,680
.

429
00:23:18,680 --> 00:23:19,680
.

430
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:21,680
.

431
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:22,680
.

432
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:23,680
.

433
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:24,680
.

434
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,680
.

435
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:55,660
I'll see you next time.

436
00:23:55,680 --> 00:24:25,660
Thank you.

